        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e057cf62-cb46-5bfe-9d6d-0b7d914aaeed",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Monopoly, King of Tokyo, The Landlord's Game\n- People: Richard Garfield\n- Concepts: Board games, tabletop games, dice, cards, boards, property trading, Chance cards, Community Chest cards, tax squares, jail\n\nFacts:\n- The Landlord's Game is the inspiration for the board game Monopoly.\n- King of Tokyo was designed by Richard Garfield and released in 2011.\n- King of Tokyo is a tabletop game that uses custom dice, cards, and boards.\n- Monopoly is a board game in which players roll two six-sided dice to move around the board, buy and trade properties, and develop them with houses and hotels.\n- Monopoly allows players to gain or lose money through Chance cards, Community Chest cards, and tax squares.\n- Monopoly can send players to jail, and players cannot move from jail until they meet one of several conditions.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ba2375d3-eb35-5d9d-958c-ec35d9c0a87a",
        "text": "Page: Monopoly (game). Sentence: Monopoly is a board game where players roll two six-sided dice to move around the game-board buying and trading properties, and then develop them with houses and hotels.\nPage: Monopoly (game). Sentence: Money can also be gained or lost through Chance and Community Chest cards, and tax squares; players can end up in jail, which they cannot move from until they have met one of several conditions.\nPage: King of Tokyo. Sentence: King of Tokyo is a tabletop game using custom dice, cards, and boards, designed by Richard Garfield and released in 2011.\nPage: The Landlord's Game. Sentence: It is the inspiration for the board game \"Monopoly\".",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
